### Practical 9: In-Memory Caching & Query Optimization (node-cache)
### Course: Advanced Web Development Frameworks (ITUE301)
### CHARUSAT - Faculty of Technology & Engineering
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client / Thunder Client / Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### =========================================================================
### 1. Health Check
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 2. Login to Obtain Bearer Token
### =========================================================================
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Store token from login response
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### =========================================================================
### 3. Supplementary Problem 2: Check Initial Cache Stats
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/stats
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 4. Step 3: GET /tasks (First Request -> Cache MISS)
### Notice response header: X-Cache: MISS
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 5. Step 5: GET /tasks (Immediate Second Request -> Cache HIT)
### Notice response header: X-Cache: HIT (Significantly faster response time)
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 6. Step 5: GET /tasks (Third Request -> Cache HIT)
### Record this in your lab journal response time table
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 7. Supplementary Problem 1: Single-Task Caching (GET /tasks/:id)
### First call -> Cache MISS
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/64c8f1a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 8. Supplementary Problem 1: Single-Task Caching (GET /tasks/:id)
### Second call -> Cache HIT
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/64c8f1a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 9. Step 4: Write Operation - POST /tasks (Creates task & Invalidates Cache)
### =========================================================================
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Evaluate in-memory caching performance",
  "description": "Demonstrate cache hit/miss ratio and response latency reduction with node-cache",
  "priority": "high"
}

@createdTaskId = {{createTask.response.body.data._id}}

### =========================================================================
### 10. Verify Cache Invalidation after POST
### This request MUST yield X-Cache: MISS (proves stale data is never served)
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 11. Write Operation - PUT /tasks/:id (Updates task & Invalidates Cache)
### =========================================================================
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createdTaskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Evaluate in-memory caching performance (Completed)",
  "completed": true
}

### =========================================================================
### 12. Write Operation - DELETE /tasks/:id (Deletes task & Invalidates Cache)
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createdTaskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 13. Step 6: Temporarily Disable Caching (Compare Uncached Requests)
### Using ?no_cache=true query parameter to measure uncached baseline
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?no_cache=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 14. Supplementary Problem 2: Inspect Final Cache Metrics & Hit Ratio
### =========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/stats
Accept: application/json

### =========================================================================
### 15. Reset Cache & Metrics
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/cache/clear
Accept: application/json
